# Configure Server

This guide covers the minimum settings to run `loom-server` and validate readiness.

## 1. Set core runtime configuration

```bash
export LOOM_SERVER_HTTP_HOST="0.0.0.0"
export LOOM_SERVER_HTTP_PORT="8080"
export LOOM_SERVER_HTTP_BASE_URL="https://loom.example.com"
export LOOM_SERVER_DB_PATH="/var/lib/loom/loom.db"
```

For local testing:

```bash
export LOOM_SERVER_AUTH_DEV_MODE=1
```

## 2. Start server

```bash
cargo run -p loom-server
```

Or use your release binary/deployment mechanism.

## 3. Validate health and metrics routes

```bash
curl -s https://loom.example.com/health | jq .
curl -s https://loom.example.com/metrics | head
```

## 4. Enable optional subsystems as needed

Examples of common additions:

- OAuth providers (`LOOM_SERVER_GITHUB_*`, `LOOM_SERVER_GOOGLE_*`, `LOOM_SERVER_OKTA_*`)
- SCIM token (`LOOM_SERVER_SCIM_TOKEN`)
- Weaver/WireGuard configuration (cluster + tunnel settings)
- SMTP for email workflows

<Callout variant="warning" title="Production guardrail">
	Never run production with `LOOM_SERVER_AUTH_DEV_MODE=1`.
</Callout>

## 5. Smoke-test user-facing surfaces

- Auth providers: `GET /auth/providers`
- Docs search: `GET /docs/search`
- API auth check (after login): `GET /auth/me`

If these pass, continue with feature-specific guides for auth, SCIM, WhatsApp, and tunnels.
